\[|x + yi - 3| = 2 |x + yi + 3|,\]so
\[(x - 3)^2 + y^2 = 4[(x + 3)^2 + y^2].\]This simplifies to $x^2 + 10x + y^2 + 9 = 0.$  Completing the square, we get
\[(x + 5)^2 + y^2 = 4^2.\]This is the circle centered at $-5$ with radius 4.

